{
 "source": "trapp",
 "book": "1CH",
 "chapter": 14,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.1",
   "range": "1CH.14.1",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "fb27aea8",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.1#p1-fb27aea8",
     "text": "{See Trapp on \"2Sa 5:11\"} {See Trapp on \"2Sa 5:12\"}",
     "anchor": "Now Hiram king of Tyre.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "2Sa 5:11",
       "ref": "2SA.5.11"
      },
      {
       "text": "2Sa 5:12",
       "ref": "2SA.5.12"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.2",
   "range": "1CH.14.2",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "176d4a56",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.2#p1-176d4a56",
     "text": "For their behoof and benefit.",
     "anchor": "Because of his people."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.3",
   "range": "1CH.14.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "8b43f637",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.3#p1-8b43f637",
     "text": "Man’s badness breaketh not off the course of God’s goodness.",
     "anchor": "And David begat more sons."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.8",
   "range": "1CH.14.8",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ef9a5d28",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.8#p1-ef9a5d28",
     "text": "But had soon enough of him; but God had a holy hand in all, to bring them to condign punishment for their late misusage of dead Saul and his sons; ascribing their successes to their gods, &c.",
     "anchor": "Went up to seek David."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.11",
   "range": "1CH.14.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "20f3102c",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.11#p1-20f3102c",
     "text": "That is, saith the Chaldee Paraphrast, As water runneth out of a broken earthen vessel.",
     "anchor": "Like the breaking forth of waters."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.12",
   "range": "1CH.14.12",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e4a5748b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.12#p1-e4a5748b",
     "text": "Their terricula bogey gods. They were now in a great fright.",
     "anchor": "And when they had left their gods there."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.13",
   "range": "1CH.14.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "fbc53152",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.13#p1-fbc53152",
     "text": "Ne accepta quidem clade resipiscunt: they were obdurate and obstinate.",
     "anchor": "And the Philistine yet again."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.14",
   "range": "1CH.14.14",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ff9dea28",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.14#p1-ff9dea28",
     "text": "Where the Philistines had placed their gods, say the Hebrews.",
     "anchor": "Against the mulberry trees."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.15",
   "range": "1CH.14.15",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "72a61d2b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.15#p1-72a61d2b",
     "text": "That is, The angel of God, saith the Chaldee.",
     "anchor": "For God."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trapp/1CH.14.17",
   "range": "1CH.14.17",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "408ac456",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "trapp/1CH.14.17#p1-408ac456",
     "text": "He grew terrible to his enemies. So did Hunniades, Scanderbeg, Charles V, &c., ita et parentes liberis plorantibus silentium non aliter imperarent quam horum praesentiam minitando: so that mothers stilled their children by these men’s names.",
     "anchor": "And the Lord brought the fear of him."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
